    20	       of L(x) equals the parity of x.  Hence L(x) mod 2 = x mod 2 is a
    21	       FREE identity — it carries no non-trivial information about primes.
    22	
    23	  (ii) Writing L(x) = x - 2*A(x) with A(x) = (x - L(x))/2 the count of
