    25	            L(x) mod 4 = (x - 2 A(x)) mod 4
    26	       so  A(x) mod 2 = ((x mod 4) - (L(x) mod 4)) / 2 (mod 2).
    27	       Therefore the *non-trivial* part of "L(x) mod 4" is exactly
    28	       A(x) mod 2.
    29	
    30	  (iii) pi(x) = A(x) - C_3(x), so pi(x) mod 2 = (A(x) mod 2) XOR
