Session 69 complete. The deep-focus Task #4 slot was already closed (S33), so per CLAUDE.md guidance I redirected to **NOVELTY_CHALLENGES.md §2.F2**.

**Result: closed-form refinement of edge E1.5.**

For every modulus m and every X with m ≪ π(X):
```
H(π(x) mod m | π(x-1) mod m, x∈[1,X]) = h_2(π(X)/X) + O(1/π(X))
```
Verified to 7-decimal-place precision at X = 10⁷ across moduli {2,4,...,1024} plus cross-checks. The "0.537 bits" of E1.5 is exposed as the X = 10⁴ special case; the constant decays with X and vanishes asymptotically — strengthening the CRT-cannot-win argument.

**Mechanism:** since π(x) − π(x−1) = 1[x prime] ∈ {0,1}, and the prime indicator is conditionally independent of the state pi(x-1) mod m when m ≪ π(X), the conditional entropy reduces to h_2 of the prime density. The m ~ π(X) regime breaks saturation as state becomes injective in x — a finite-size effect, not a structural property.

**Falsification:** F2-A (closed form) PASS; F2-B (m-saturation in regime) PASS; F2-C (literal "0.537·k linear" framing) FALSIFIED.

